diff --git a/docs/serializer.rst b/docs/serializer.rst
index 1b1da66..9d9bd23 100644
--- a/docs/serializer.rst
+++ b/docs/serializer.rst
@@ -127,6 +127,30 @@ wrong you can also use :meth:`~Serializer.loads_unsafe`:
 The first item in the returned tuple is a boolean that indicates if the
 signature was correct.
 
+
+Fallback Signatures
+--------------------
+
+Occasionally you may want to change the signing parameters of your
+application, such as the ``digest_method`` or ``key_derivation``, while
+still being able to unsign values that were signed under the old
+configuration. Pass the old configuration(s) as ``fallback_signers``
+when constructing the serializer:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    import hashlib
+    s = Serializer(
+        "secret-key",
+        fallback_signers=[{"digest_method": hashlib.sha512}],
+    )
+
+Each entry in ``fallback_signers`` may be a dict of keyword arguments
+passed to the signer class, a ``(signer_cls, kwargs)`` tuple, or a
+signer class to use with the serializer's ``signer_kwargs``. When
+unsigning, each fallback is tried in order after the primary signer
+fails.
+
 API
 ---
 
